  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Uniform Convergence [S+N]\n\nLet $f_n : [a, b] \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be a sequence of functions. Two convergence notions:\n\n- **Pointwise**: $f_n \\to f$ pointwise if for each $x$, $f_n(x) \\to f(x)$ as a number sequence. Equivalently, $\\forall x\\,\\forall \\varepsilon > 0\\,\\exists N(\\varepsilon, x)$ such that $n \\ge N \\Rightarrow |f_n(x) - f(x)| < \\varepsilon$.\n\n- **Uniform**: $f_n \\to f$ uniformly if $N$ can be chosen *independent of* $x$. Equivalently, $\\sup_{x \\in [a,b]} |f_n(x) - f(x)| \\to 0$.\n\nPointwise is too weak to preserve continuity, integration, differentiation. Uniform is exactly what makes those exchanges legal.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 29,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The classic counter-example: $f_n(x) = x^n$ on $[0, 1]$\n\nPointwise limit:\n- For $x \\in [0, 1)$, $x^n \\to 0$.\n- For $x = 1$, $1^n = 1$ for all $n$.\n\nSo $f_n \\to f$ where $f(1) = 1$ and $f(x) = 0$ for $x < 1$. The pointwise limit is **discontinuous**, even though every $f_n$ is continuous.\n\nThe convergence is **not** uniform: $\\sup_{x \\in [0,1]} |x^n - f(x)| = 1$ for every $n$. Note the supremum is *not attained* — at $x = 1$ the difference is $0$, and on $[0, 1)$ the difference is $x^n$, which only climbs to $1$ in the limit $x \\to 1^-$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_grid : np_to_list(np_linspace(0, 1, 200))$\nn_show : [1, 2, 5, 20, 100]$\nplot_args : [color=\"blue\", line_width=1, name=\"n=1\", lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^1)), x_grid))]$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"cornflowerblue\", line_width=1, name=\"n=1\",\n  lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^1)), x_grid)),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=1, name=\"n=2\",\n  lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^2)), x_grid)),\n  color=\"orange\", line_width=1, name=\"n=5\",\n  lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^5)), x_grid)),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"n=20\",\n  lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^20)), x_grid)),\n  color=\"purple\", line_width=2, name=\"n=100\",\n  lines(x_grid, map(lambda([x], float(x^100)), x_grid)),\n  title=\"x^n on [0,1] — pointwise limit is discontinuous\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"x^n\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 30,
      "outputs": [
        {
